.DS_Store
__pycache__/
system/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
config.yaml
# profile.yaml is intentionally NOT ignored — it holds non-secret identity/prefs
# (name, full_name, timezone) and is committed so it travels across machines.
system/schedule.json
system/question-bank-upstream.md
skill/life-legacy
state/synthesis/
state/agent_tasks/
# Local execution state: durable on one machine, never vault content. Job
# records are metadata-only; opaque payload sidecars can contain private input.
state/jobs/
# Update-check cache (lifehug#84) — same class as state/jobs/: local
# execution state written by update.py, never vault content, regenerated by
# the next --check/--apply.
state/update_check.json
state/last_update.json
# The learning-failure ledger is per-vault runtime state. A test or dev run
# against the checkout must never end up committing one (issue #225 — the
# suite once wrote it via a stubbed timeline_interaction, and `git add -A`
# picked it up). Defense in depth: the suite is also guarded to leave the
# checkout clean (tests/test_learning_failures_leak.py).
state/learning_failures.jsonl
# Connector secrets (v106). The ledger JSONL itself IS committed — it is
# owner-only metadata state like the rest of state/. The body cache is
# committed too (v108 — owner relaxed raw storage); only secrets stay ignored.
state/connectors/gmail_token.json
state/connectors/gmail_client_secrets.json
